    "question": {
      ":question/id": "ba11813c-a0fd-59e9-8d3e-e9a1b855fa7d",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following is an upper triangular matrix?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $C$ is a matrix for which all entries *below* the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nHence, it is an upper triangular matrix. \n\nBy contrast, matrices $A$, $B$, $D$, and $E$ each have at least one non-zero entry below the diagonal:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nE=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, they are not upper triangular matrices.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
